## Reproduces the F1 review finding directly: a step=1 basis (b-spline)
## whose periodic axis is below validPeriodicBicubicMeshDim's true safety
## floor (see gmanpatchpolyobjectmanager.cpp). validBicubicMeshDim's
## periodic branch used to accept any nu>=step, which at step=1 let nu=1
## through -- GMANBasis::offset's periodic wraparound (a single `i-=nu`,
## not a true modulo) only stays in [0,nu) for nu>=3 at step=1, so nu=1
## read one point past the 4-point "P" array below (ASan
## heap-buffer-overflow, confirmed against the unfixed validator). Every
## fixture elsewhere in this suite uses the default Bezier basis
## (step=3), where the bug was vacuous -- this is the only fixture that
## exercises a step=1 basis's periodic floor at all.
##
## A trailing Sphere follows AGENTS.md's "RIB authoring" section, "The
## desync convention."
Display "patchmesh_bspline_periodic_baddim.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 200 200 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [45]
Clipping 0.5 50
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
LightSource "ambientlight" 1 "intensity" [0.6]
Sides 2
Surface "matte" "Ka" [1] "Kd" [0]
Basis "b-spline" 1 "b-spline" 1
AttributeBegin
	Translate -1 0 0
	PatchMesh "bicubic" 1 "periodic" 4 "nonperiodic" "P" [
		-0.3 -0.3 0
		-0.3 -0.1 0
		-0.3  0.1 0
		-0.3  0.3 0
	]
AttributeEnd
AttributeBegin
	Translate 1 0 0
	Sphere 0.5 -0.5 0.5 360
AttributeEnd
WorldEnd
